---
source: crates/page/tests/corpus.rs
expression: "dumps(&page, &list)"
---
== dom ==
#document
  #doctype html
  html lang="en"
    head
      "\n"
      meta charset="utf-8"
      "\n"
      title
        "A plain article"
      "\n"
      link rel="stylesheet" href="article.css"
      "\n"
    "\n"
    body
      "\n"
      header
        p class="kicker"
          "Field notes"
        h1
          "Why small browsers matter"
        "\n"
        p class="byline"
          "By A. Writer, "
          time
            "21 October"
      "\n"
      article
        "\n"
        p
          "A browser is mostly a "
          em
            "reading"
          " machine. Most of what people open is text: news, documentation,\nrecipes and long essays. If a small engine gets "
          strong
            "that"
          " right, it is already useful."
        "\n"
        h2
          "What it takes"
        "\n"
        p
          "Reading needs a parser that forgives broken markup, a cascade that applies styles in the\nright order, and "
          a href="#layout"
            "flow layout"
          " that wraps lines where people expect."
        "\n"
        ul
          "\n"
          li
            "Parse the page as it streams in."
          "\n"
          li
            "Style it with the cascade."
          "\n"
          li
            "Lay out blocks and lines, then paint."
          "\n"
        "\n"
        blockquote
          p
            "Simple things should be simple."
        "\n"
        h2 id="layout"
          "Layout"
        "\n"
        p
          "Blocks stack down the page; their vertical margins collapse. Inside a block, text and inline\nboxes fill "
          code
            "line boxes"
          " from left to right."
        "\n"
        ol
          li
            "First"
          li
            "Second"
        "\n"
        p
          img src="two.png" alt="two colour bars" width="40" height="20"
          " A picture sits on the line like a word."
        "\n"
        hr
        "\n"
        p class="footnote"
          "Thanks for reading."
        "\n"
      "\n\n\n"

